The model (CC BY 4.0), MobileSAM and Segment Anything (Apache-2.0)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
The app downloads microsam-vit-t-lm-encoder.onnx and microsam-vit-t-lm-decoder.onnx
(models/microsam.manifest.json): micro-sam's "SAM LM Generalist (ViT-T)" (vit_t_lm,
BioImage.IO faithful-chicken 1.1) by Anwai Archit, Constantin Pape and the micro-sam
contributors, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Archit, A. et
al. Segment Anything for Microscopy. Nature Methods 22, 579-591 (2025),
https://doi.org/10.1038/s41592-024-02580-4.

Modified (CC BY 4.0 section 3(a)(1)(B)): converted to ONNX by validation/export_onnx.py. The
encoder is exported as micro-sam's PyTorch path runs it: TinyViT's cached attention biases
(Attention.ab) are the zero cache MobileSAM's builder computes before the checkpoint is loaded,
and that cache is folded into the graph. The trained attention biases of the checkpoint
(attention_biases) are therefore not used by the exported encoder; every other weight is the
checkpoint's.

The model is fine-tuned from MobileSAM, Copyright (c) Chaoning Zhang and contributors
(https://github.com/ChaoningZhang/MobileSAM), itself distilled from Segment Anything,
Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates
(https://github.com/facebookresearch/segment-anything). Both are licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0; the full text is in LICENSE-APACHE-2.0, shipped beside this file
and beside the model files on Hugging Face. The encoder graph is MobileSAM's TinyViT and the
decoder graph is MobileSAM's SamOnnxModel (mobile_sam/utils/onnx.py, from
segment_anything/utils/onnx.py), both traced into the ONNX files; neither project ships a NOTICE
file.

